WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:03.949
Roxy flew to Mountain View Hotel.

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:06.587
In the parking lot, guests were gathered together.

3
00:00:06.588 --> 00:00:08.424
They all looked angry.

4
00:00:08.425 --> 00:00:10.508
Roxy entered the lobby.

5
00:00:10.509 --> 00:00:12.936
"Yikes!" she thought.

6
00:00:12.937 --> 00:00:15.409
"There's dust everywhere."

7
00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:19.295
Detective Smith was standing with another man.

8
00:00:19.296 --> 00:00:24.052
"Detective Smith, don't dust stand there," Roxy said.

9
00:00:24.053 --> 00:00:26.552
"Grab a dust pan!"

10
00:00:26.553 --> 00:00:33.164
"Ha-ha, Rocket Girl," Detective Smith said. "Very—ah-choo!"

11
00:00:33.165 --> 00:00:36.294
"Thank goodness you're here, Rocket Girl!" Mr. Denton said.

12
00:00:36.295 --> 00:00:37.880
"I'm the owner of the hotel.

13
00:00:37.881 --> 00:00:40.474
Can you do something about this dust?"

14
00:00:40.475 --> 00:00:44.805
"Maybe," Roxy said. "Where did it come from?"

15
00:00:44.806 --> 00:00:47.321
"I don't know," Mr. Denton said.

16
00:00:47.322 --> 00:00:50.471
"But I must get rid of it—it's ruining my business."

17
00:00:50.472 --> 00:00:54.115
"Did you call a cleaning service?" Detective Smith asked.

18
00:00:54.116 --> 00:00:55.681
Mr. Denton nodded.

19
00:00:55.682 --> 00:00:58.337
"I left a message with my new cleaner, Tanya Tidy.

20
00:00:58.338 --> 00:01:00.636
I hope she calls me back soon."

21
00:01:00.637 --> 00:01:05.195
"Some guests are missing valuables, Rocket Girl," Detective Smith said.

22
00:01:05.196 --> 00:01:08.827
"But we can't look for clues until the dust is gone."

23
00:01:08.828 --> 00:01:11.699
"Let's open all the windows," Roxy said.

24
00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:21.570
"Then you two, go outside."

25
00:01:21.571 --> 00:01:24.297
Soon Roxy was alone inside.

26
00:01:24.298 --> 00:01:31.621
Whoosh! She used her super breath to blow away the dust.

27
00:01:31.622 --> 00:01:34.583
Detective Smith and Mr. Denton returned to the lobby.

28
00:01:34.584 --> 00:01:38.455
"Nice job, Rocket Girl," Detective Smith said.

29
00:01:38.456 --> 00:01:41.229
"But while you were cleaning, I got a call.

30
00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:45.198
Victoria Cash's mansion just filled up with dust!"

31
00:01:45.241 --> 00:01:51.967
"I bet it's another burglary!" Roxy said.

32
00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:56.430
When Roxy arrived, Victoria Cash and her daughter, Ruby, were standing outside.

33
00:01:56.431 --> 00:01:59.318
They were covering their faces with cloth and coughing.

34
00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:02.583
"I heard about the dust in your mansion," Roxy said.

35
00:02:02.584 --> 00:02:04.448
"Is anything missing?"

36
00:02:04.449 --> 00:02:09.541
"Yes!" Victoria said. "Ruby's rubies!"

37
00:02:09.542 --> 00:02:11.554
Ruby held up a fancy doll.

38
00:02:11.555 --> 00:02:15.694
"Somebody stole Lillian's ruby tiara!"

39
00:02:15.695 --> 00:02:20.165
Victoria bit her lip. "I don't know what else is missing.

40
00:02:20.166 --> 00:02:23.754
There was too much dust to see anything!"

41
00:02:23.755 --> 00:02:31.484
"I'll check it out," Roxy said. "Wait here."

42
00:02:31.485 --> 00:02:34.490
The mansion was filled with dust.

43
00:02:34.491 --> 00:02:37.947
As Roxy walked around, she thought she heard something.

44
00:02:37.948 --> 00:02:39.854
She used her super hearing.

45
00:02:39.855 --> 00:02:42.793
Humm. Humm.

46
00:02:42.794 --> 00:02:51.291
"It sounds like a . . ." Roxy followed the sound to a back room.

47
00:02:51.292 --> 00:02:53.613
"A robot vacuum!"

48
00:02:53.614 --> 00:02:58.028
The machine was circling the floor, spraying out thick dust.

49
00:02:58.029 --> 00:03:03.180
Roxy coughed.

50
00:03:03.181 --> 00:03:07.520
Then, wiping dust off a window, she spotted a van parked outside.

51
00:03:07.521 --> 00:03:11.815
"Tanya Tidy's Cleaning Service," Roxy thought.

52
00:03:11.816 --> 00:03:15.379
"Mr. Denton uses that service too!"

53
00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:18.974
Cleaners in black masks were standing around a tall woman.

54
00:03:18.975 --> 00:03:21.104
She was wearing a maid's uniform.

55
00:03:21.105 --> 00:03:24.332
Bags stuffed with stolen goods lay on the ground.

56
00:03:24.333 --> 00:03:26.877
So did several cleaning tools.

57
00:03:26.878 --> 00:03:31.584
A cleaner suddenly glanced toward the window.

58
00:03:31.585 --> 00:03:36.945
"Uh-oh, boss. Rocket Girl!"

